er":"Jeff Ulbrich"},{"season":2023,"team":"TB","distance":0.3239,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Todd Bowles"},{"season":2024,"team":"NE","distance":0.335,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2025,"team":"DAL","distance":0.3664,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2022,"team":"CLE","distance":0.3713,"shared":4,"play_caller":null}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Cardinals are 3-8 through week 11 of the 2026 season and have been outscored 323 to 191. Neither side has held up so far, with the offense 25th in EPA per play and the defense 31st in EPA allowed. What sets them apart is the 3rd fewest backs in the backfield in the league.","offense":"The Cardinals offense has been well below average by EPA per play so far. Their run and pass mix has stayed close to what game situations call for. Schematically, they stand out for the 3rd fewest backs in the backfield and the 3rd lowest play-action rate in the league. Jacoby Brissett has run the passing game and leaned heavily on Trey McBride, who has drawn 29% of the targets.","defense":"The Cardinals defense has been one of the worst in the league by EPA allowed per play so far. It has been much better against the run than the pass, ranking 11th and 32nd. Josh Sweat has been as productive as expected, but the bigger surprise is Budda Baker, who has 3.5 sacks, after doing little as a pass rusher a year ago. Their scheme has been fairly conventional, and the closest thing to a signature is a number of defenders in the box that ranks 4th highest in the league.","special":"The Cardinals have been one of the most conservative teams on fourth down, going for it on only 25% of their short-yardage chances. Their kickers have made 92% of field goals, which is well above average. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into tight ends, about 10% of the money on the books.","players":"Jacoby Brissett has played nearly every snap at quarterback and thrown for 1,719 yards. Trey McBride has been the clear top target with 29% of the looks and 689 receiving yards. The backfield has been a committee led by Tyler Allgeier and Jeremiyah Love. On defense, Budda Baker leads the team with 3.5 sacks.","coaching":"Mike LaFleur is calling the offense as head coach and Nick Rallis is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2022 Jets under Mike LaFleur and the 2024 Raiders. Their defense looks most like the 2024 Jets under Jeff Ulbrich and the 2023 Buccaneers under Todd Bowles.","trends":"The offense went from 23rd in EPA per play in 2025 to 25th so far this season, about where it was. The defense moved from 27th in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 31st so far this season, a modest decline. The biggest change in approach was number of defenders in the box, which went from 6.13 to 6.52.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}